REASON
The per-tick speed draw was repeated in three places and cached in the instance-scoped
'n', which served no purpose beyond the tick that set it; it is now a function. The
commented-out document.hidden block is removed — it had been dead since 2021 and its
empty if/else made the live branch read as conditional when it was not. 'self' is
dropped, having become unused once recursion stopped going through the public method,
and 'type' becomes a local of writeText(), its only reader. this.stop is added to the
non-writable list so the new method matches the other three.

